    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="namespacetle92466ed_1_1CTRL__INT__THRESH" kindref="compound">CTRL_INT_THRESH</ref> register bit definitions. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Per datasheet Rev 1.2 \u00a75.3.3.13 p.97. Holds the integrator threshold used after a setpoint change or when the PWM frequency controller is activated; a greater threshold yields a longer on-time (\u00a74.6.2.3). bits 15:9 Reserved (read-only) bits 8:0 INT_THRESH 9-bit integrator threshold. The programmed value is positive; the <emphasis>effective</emphasis> threshold may still go negative because it is referenced to the lowest deviation integral captured during the on-phase. <ref refid="namespacetle92466ed_1_1CH__CTRL__REG_1a4546d2f98485d1e179146fb36f0b99b0" kindref="member">CH_CTRL_REG::MIN_INT_THRESH_MASK</ref> bounds that.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="warning"><para>This register has <bold>no PERIOD_MANT field</bold>. It was previously documented here as <computeroutput>PERIOD_MANT</computeroutput> in bits 15:8 with a signed 8-bit <computeroutput>INT_THRESH</computeroutput> in 7:0, and manual on-time mode was described as &quot;set PERIOD_MANT=0 here&quot;. Per \u00a74.6.2.3 the PWM frequency controller is disabled by zeroing <computeroutput>PERIOD_MANT</computeroutput> in the <bold><ref refid="namespacetle92466ed_1_1PERIOD" kindref="compound">PERIOD</ref></bold> register instead. Writing this register through the old layout put the seed in the wrong bits and drove reserved bits 15:9. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
